How your listed factors affect fracture/fall risk
- Age 55: younger than routine screening age for everyone (DEXA usually at ≥65), but screening is indicated earlier when additional risk factors exist.
- Atrial fibrillation: can increase fall risk if you have palpitations/syncope; anticoagulation raises bleeding risk with falls.
