Key issues to cover with Dr. Chen (and why)
- Do I need a DEXA scan now?  
  - Why: DEXA is the definitive test to quantify osteopenia vs osteoporosis. Guidelines often recommend routine screening at older ages (e.g., age 65 for women) but earlier testing is appropriate with risk factors (prior low-trauma fracture, long-term steroid use, diabetes, other secondary causes). Your age (55) + risk factors may justify testing.
