Lifestyle and supplementation to discuss
- Calcium intake: total (diet + supplements) generally targeted to about 1,000–1,200 mg/day for adults (ask your PCP for individualized guidance). Try to prioritize dietary calcium; supplement only if needed.  
- Vitamin D: aim for an adequate 25‑OH D level (many clinicians target ≥20–30 ng/mL; your PCP may aim for ~30). Supplement dose depends on baseline level.  
- Weight-bearing and strength/balance exercises (PT or exercise program) to reduce fall and fracture risk.  
- Fall-risk reduction: vision check, home safety, review of medications that cause dizziness, balance training.  
- Smoking cessation and limiting heavy alcohol use.

When to consider medication (high-level thresholds)
- Osteoporosis defined as T-score ≤ −2.5 — typically treat.  
- Osteopenia (T-score −1.0 to −2.5) — treat if:
  - Prior fragility fracture OR
