C. How your specifics affect decisions
- Age 55: routine DEXA is generally recommended at age ≥65 for women without risk factors, but for people younger than that it’s appropriate when they have risk factors (diabetes, secondary causes, prior fracture, significant fall risk). Your diabetes and retinopathy increase risk.
