Quick context summary I’ll use below
- Age 55. History of atrial fibrillation. You gave an INR of 1.2 (suggests you may be on warfarin and currently subtherapeutic — please confirm your anticoagulant).
- Taking metformin 500 mg twice daily. Seasonal allergies; you take calcium and vitamin D supplements. History of retinopathy.
