- Can we address fall risk and vision/safety issues related to retinopathy?

Suggested questions if you do contact Northwest Orthopedics
- Do you accept referrals for medical management of low bone density, or do you focus on surgical/orthopedic care?
- If I have no fractures but have osteopenia and diabetes, would you evaluate me or refer me back to endocrinology/PCP for medical management?
- If I have a fragility fracture, what is your pathway for coordinating surgical/medical care?

Things to bring to the appointment
- A list of medications (including supplements and doses)
- Any prior DEXA reports
- Records of prior fractures or major falls
- Recent labs (A1c, creatinine) if available

Red flags that need quicker attention
- New bone pain or suspected fracture after a fall
- Signs of bleeding or if your INR is out of range and you are on warfarin — contact your cardiology/PCP right away
- Sudden visual changes (given retinopathy)

